<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tranquebar Mission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1706">1706</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharangambadi">Tranquebar</a> Mission was the first Protestant mission in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in 1706 at the Danish colony of Tranquebar by the German Lutherans <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartholomaus-ziegenbalg">Bartholomäus Ziegenbalg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-plutschau">Heinrich Plütschau</a> at the request of King Frederick IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. It set up schools and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press and produced the first Tamil translation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-testament">New Testament</a>.</p></div>
